# This repository is developed on Windows with core.autocrlf=true, which rewrites checked-out
# files to CRLF. That is harmless for most files and FATAL for a shell script that has to run on
# Linux: a `#!/usr/bin/env bash` shebang becomes `bash\r`, and the kernel looks for an interpreter
# whose name ends in a carriage return. The self-hosted runner's entrypoint failed exactly this
# way, restarting in a loop with exit 127, while git had been printing
# "LF will be replaced by CRLF" on every add.
#
# Anything executed by Linux keeps LF regardless of platform or local git configuration.
*.sh    text eol=lf
*.bash  text eol=lf

# Dockerfiles are read by the daemon rather than a shell, but a heredoc or a line continuation
# inside one has the same problem, so they are pinned too.
Dockerfile      text eol=lf
*.dockerfile    text eol=lf

# PowerShell is Windows-side and reads either ending; left to the platform default deliberately
# rather than pinned, so nothing here fights the editor.
